WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:03.280
The virus was swift and deadly.

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:05.163
After emerging near your home

00:00:05.163 --> 00:00:07.600
in New York City, it spread.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.640
First to London, then to Tokyo,

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.732
eventually wiping out more than

00:00:12.732 --> 00:00:16.010
99% of the global population.

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:17.668
But you...

00:00:17.668 --> 00:00:19.043
you were lucky.

00:00:19.043 --> 00:00:21.310
You were one of the few thousand people

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:24.660
on Earth with immunity who survived.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.523
So, now what?

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.790
Your first step is to stock up.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:35.950
An average midsize supermarket

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:39.700
can sustain one person for about 55 years.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:43.840
63, if you're cool with
eating the cat and dog food.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.410
As you scan the aisles,
look for canned food,

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:50.570
some of which can last
for up to several decades,

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:52.190
and bottled water.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:54.860
Because once the power grid goes down,

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:57.580
your municipal water supply will run dry

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:58.946
in a matter of weeks

00:00:58.946 --> 00:01:00.621
or even days.

00:01:00.621 --> 00:01:02.780
You'll also want to grab some superglue

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.280
in case you get injured.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.170
It can easily seal wounds
in the absence of stitches.

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:10.253
And make sure to hit up hospitals,

00:01:10.253 --> 00:01:12.640
pharmacies, and even vet offices

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.073
for antibiotics and pain killers.

00:01:15.073 --> 00:01:17.352
Vets treat animals with many of the

00:01:17.352 --> 00:01:20.000
same medicines that we use for humans,

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.480
such as the pain reliever hydrocodone

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:25.160
and the antibiotic doxycycline.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.810
Once you're packed, you'll
want to hit the road.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:30.330
Because without electricity
to cool the fuel

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:34.140
inside nuclear reactors,
pressure could build up

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:37.610
and cause the reactor's
containment building to fail.

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:41.260
Especially if it's old or
it was poorly maintained.

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:43.600
And that could release toxic radiation

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.920
within a 50-mile radius or greater.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.595
And even if your city or town

00:01:48.595 --> 00:01:50.303
isn't near one of these plants,

00:01:50.303 --> 00:01:52.680
you'll still want to seek isolation.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.500
Because in the aftermath
of the apocalypse,

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:59.510
there will be decaying corpses
strewn about the streets.

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:02.010
Oh, yeah. It's gonna stink.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:04.510
But they'll also attract animal scavengers

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:07.560
and infectious bacteria
that could harm or kill you

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.210
if you get too close.

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:11.526
So, yeah, a country home

00:02:11.526 --> 00:02:13.740
is looking pretty good right now.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.348
Though it'll be tough to figure out

00:02:15.348 --> 00:02:17.400
exactly where to settle.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.580
You'll need to be close to fresh water

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:22.860
but also far away from major rivers,

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:25.404
because many dams could
eventually collapse

00:02:25.404 --> 00:02:27.710
without anyone to maintain them.

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:29.820
You'll also want to be near fertile soil

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:31.420
so you can grow your own food

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.910
once your grocery supply runs out.

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:37.100
And, of course, you'll want
to be at least 50 miles

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.090
from a nuclear power plant.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:42.450
So somewhere north of Edison, New Jersey,

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.850
would probably be a good bet.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.690
After settling in, you'll need

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:48.890
a steady supply of drinking water.

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:50.533
So it's a good thing purifying

00:02:50.533 --> 00:02:53.810
creek or lake water is surprisingly easy.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:55.620
You can bring it to a boil,

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:57.803
fill up clear plastic water bottles

00:02:57.803 --> 00:02:59.350
no larger than a liter

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:01.058
and stick them in direct sunlight

00:03:01.058 --> 00:03:02.641
for at least six hours,

00:03:02.641 --> 00:03:06.600
or add a few drops of a
5% liquid bleach solution

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.210
to a liter of water.

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:11.680
But farming your own food
would be a lot tougher.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.610
If you're able to scavenge a gun

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:15.930
or a bow and arrow, you could hunt.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:19.210
There are over 100,000 deer in New Jersey,

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:22.150
which is more than 11 per square mile.

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:24.640
And each one could keep you satisfied

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:28.240
(or, at least, alive)
for two weeks or more.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.640
But wouldn't it be easier just to farm?

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.133
Assuming you could plant
the right crops, yes.

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:36.750
Corn, for example, might be everywhere.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.943
But many modern varieties are hybrids

00:03:38.943 --> 00:03:41.400
and often can't reproduce on their own,

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.230
so they won't grow from
one year to the next.

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:46.038
That's why you'll want to scavenge

00:03:46.038 --> 00:03:49.613
seeds of heirloom crops,
which reproduce naturally.

00:03:49.613 --> 00:03:52.690
Try searching small
farms, backyard gardens,

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:55.150
and garden centers for beans, potatoes,

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:57.290
and some kind of leafy green.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:58.585
That way you'll have a supply

00:03:58.585 --> 00:04:01.750
of protein, carbs, and lots of vitamins.

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:03.483
Now, with crops in the ground,

00:04:03.483 --> 00:04:05.260
things will be looking up.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:08.910
You know, relative to life
in post-apocalyptic times.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.020
But you know what would make it better?

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:12.350
Electricity.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.483
You could store perishable foods,

00:04:14.483 --> 00:04:16.083
like the deer you killed.

00:04:16.083 --> 00:04:18.800
Not to mention have light,
heat, running water,

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.870
and whatever else might help
you live more comfortably.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.870
At first, you can
scavenge motor generators

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:27.380
from roadwork or construction sites

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:29.338
and siphon gasoline out of

00:04:29.338 --> 00:04:31.600
abandoned cars to power them.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.325
But eventually you'll want to nab

00:04:33.325 --> 00:04:36.108
some solar panels along with big batteries

00:04:36.108 --> 00:04:38.270
to store the power they produce.

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:41.210
Abandoned golf carts might
be a good place to look.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:44.690
They're powered by deep-cycle
lead-acid batteries,

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:46.750
which you can discharge many times

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:50.217
without significantly
shortening their lifespan.

00:04:50.217 --> 00:04:54.000
Aah. Now you can finally relax.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.320
All that's left is
repopulating the planet.

